Stop saying just "kawaii" 🌸 Compliment someone in Japanese like this 👇

💬 5 phrases to steal today:
• かわいいですね (kawaii desu ne) = That's so cute!
• かっこいいですよ (kakkoii desu yo) = You're handsome / cool!
• すてきですね (suteki desu ne) = That's lovely!
• ありがとうございます (arigatou gozaimasu) = Thank you very much
• うれしい (ureshii) = I'm so happy!

💡 Pro tip: add も (mo) = "too" to return a compliment instantly.
アレックスさんも かっこいいですよ = You're handsome too, Alex!

👇 Which one would you say first? Comment it!
